  "case": "The readers are funders whom board members will meet to talk about Harborlight's sixth site. They need to believe that more adults want classes than five sites can serve, and that a site at Eastgate would meet much of that need. The strongest evidence is enrollment growth from 936 to 1,148 learners. At year end 287 adults were still on the waitlist, mostly at Eastgate and Riverside, and the average wait was nine weeks. Results back this up: 68% of learners who stayed at least 12 weeks gained a reading level, and 71 learners earned a high school equivalency credential. Funders will ask whether the work runs well and what it costs. The answer is 214 volunteer tutors, 11 staff, a mix of funding sources and a cost of $1,237 per learner. The ask is $190,000, the increase from $1,420,000 to a $1,610,000 budget, to pay for the Eastgate site and two site coordinators.",
